WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.455
Hi, I'm Truffle!

00:00:02.455 --> 00:00:05.563
Qwen3.8-LiveTranslate interprets speech while it's still being spoken.

00:00:05.563 --> 00:00:09.447
Here's how it's built, and how its lag is measured.

00:00:11.142 --> 00:00:15.448
The idea: instead of three models in a row, one causal sequence

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:19.036
holds audio, video, source text and translation, interleaved in time.

00:00:19.036 --> 00:00:20.830
No hand-offs to wait on.

00:00:22.592 --> 00:00:26.583
Video and audio stream into the Thinker, a hybrid mixture of experts.

00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:30.907
It writes source text and translation into the same sequence, in time order.

00:00:31.328 --> 00:00:34.282
Turns are now cut by speaker, not by silence.

00:00:34.282 --> 00:00:37.893
Source and translation come out aligned, each with a speaker label.

00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:42.096
The Talker turns the translation into speech, cloning the voice from the

00:00:42.096 --> 00:00:44.933
live input, so each speaker keeps their own timbre.

00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:48.148
How is lag scored?

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.477
As the average gap between two staircases.

00:00:50.897 --> 00:00:53.976
D i: how much source audio had arrived when word i came out.

00:00:54.396 --> 00:00:57.247
D star i: when an oracle, perfectly in sync with the

00:00:57.247 --> 00:00:58.284
speaker, would say it.

00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:03.996
The result: average lag fell from two point eight to two point

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:08.150
three seconds, and quality rose too, from eighty-three to eighty-five point seven.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.535
Usually those two trade.

00:01:11.092 --> 00:01:15.840
The catch: that's nineteen of sixty supported languages, all through English or Chinese.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.857
And the architecture is disclosed as a diagram and a sentence.

00:01:21.142 --> 00:01:24.161
A lag number alone means nothing in interpretation.

00:01:24.161 --> 00:01:27.180
The result is lag and quality improving together.

00:01:28.692 --> 00:01:32.872
To recap: one interleaved sequence, turns cut by speaker, and less

00:01:32.872 --> 00:01:34.391
lag without losing quality.

00:01:34.811 --> 00:01:36.913
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:36.913 --> 00:01:37.513
I'm Truffle.

00:01:37.513 --> 00:01:37.814
Bye!
